Damnit damnit damnit damnit!

I had such a great game going.  I'd done the Mines and Sobokan, Medusa,
and the Castle.  I got a wand of wishing and didn't even use it.  Next
time I'll wish for a freakin potion of paralysis, that sounds like the
best way to beat Kaen.

I'd found an insanely good bones file in the Rogue Level, which was
weird because I didn't know you could leave bones files there.  And
apparently there was an insane bones file in the VotD.  When I went
down to check it out there were a bunch of bone devils, a black dragon,
Jubliex and Yeenghou and that was just by the stairs up!

Anway, I had 140 hp and -13 AC.  Speed boots, MR, reflection, free
action, levitation rings.  I had wwalking boots but they weren't fire
proofed.  I went down to Master Kaen's level just to check it out.
Then he TP's next to next to me and takes like 40 hp off my life.  I
run away.  I heal and get some wands of sleep out because I heard sleep
is the way to go with Kaen if you can't wand of death him right away
and obviously he was already awake and had th Eyes.

I went back down and burned Elbereth.  Tried sleeping Kaen but it
didn't work so I ran away again.  Healed.  I was down to my last POW
points but wasn't paying attention.

Went back down.  This time I put on the ring of levitation and tried to
get to an area surronded by lava.  Except I couldn't.  Every area of
lava wasn't big enough except on the side of the screen (I went left
from the stairs).

Eventually Kaen caught me as I tried to get to a lava-locked square and
beat me to a blood pulp.


Well, actually, it wasn't eventually it happened really fast.  He beat
me like a red-headed step child.

In retrospect I should've brought potions of paralysis or wished for
them or something.  Though in my defense I only saw one potion of
paralysis that game.  And I didn't know that would work with him.  I
went down thinking my options were wand of death (didn't have and
didn't want to wish for it), sleep + levitation.  So I went with sleep
plus levitation.  Should've actually refreshed my sleep spell first,
instead of using wands.

(Looking at that map again I should've gone right.)

Joeb, neutral female human Monk


